<title>GERMANY: VW says 1996 ordinary activity profit up.</title>
<headline>VW says 1996 ordinary activity profit up.</headline>
<dateline>WOLFSBURG, Germany 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities	1,972 vs  1,113</p>
<p>    Parent income from ord. activities     1,128 vs    560</p>
<p>    Group cash flow			     11,088 vs 10,400</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German carmaker is Volkswagen AG, Europe's largest carmaker. VW said the group cash flow figure was a slight improvement over the figure reported on February 25 when it released the following data:</p>
<p>Group vehicle sales (thousands/units)  3,992 vs  3,607</p>
<p>    Group sales				  100,123 vs 88,119</p>
<p>    Group net profit				 678 vs    336</p>
<p>    Parent net profit				630 vs    410</p>
<p>    Group investments			   15,279 vs 13,072</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
